   * walk is written out eight levels deep, since the notation has no loop;
   * that is ROADMAP 3.4's line, kept, and settled for this with Hans on
   * 2026-09-30 after both ways were prototyped. A value stops early at an
   * array of `char` it starts, if it is a string, and at a struct it
   * starts, if it is one; that is how a string fills an array and a struct
   * value fills a struct. A list with no designator takes the element or
